{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\niv=[x for x in s['interpretations'] if x['id'].startswith('c5d2bc40')][0]\nprint(json.dumps(iv, indent=1))\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"id\": \"c5d2bc4029e5466da5475db36708ef10-interpretation-0\",\n \"investigation_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-question-0\",\n \"experiment_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-experiment\",\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"readindex-confirm-handler\",\n  \"readindex-confirm\",\n  \"readindex-test-context\",\n  \"pending-read-addready\",\n  \"pending-read-applied\",\n  \"pending-read-gc\",\n  \"follower-readindexresp\",\n  \"node-process-ready\",\n  \"node-readindex-admission\",\n  \"systemctx-identity\",\n  \"leader-readindex-admission\",\n  \"observer-readindex-forward\",\n  \"follower-readindex-forward\"\n ],\n \"executions\": {\n  \"c2848ac1c82f442ba305267049bbb53b\": [\n   2,\n   3,\n   4\n  ],\n  \"55e578441ac24bde9e837485d2c078a6\": [\n   1,\n   2\n  ],\n  \"c414588b5bc24b189d3df3217e37d7b7\": [\n   1\n  ],\n  \"4e011b84ec9241da9022ce3b300b5948\": [\n   1\n  ],\n  \"bd58e3e83a83442492b148168e817c4c\": [\n   0,\n   2,\n   3,\n   6,\n   7\n  ]\n },\n \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n \"rationale\": \"The conclusion remains a violated requirement and a bounded client-completion defect for remote ReadIndex requests whenever the leader confirms a later queued context before an earlier one. The source cause is unchanged: handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation returns every earlier queued request but builds each remote reply from the confirming heartbeat's Hint and HintHigh instead of that request's s.ctx, while readIndex.confirm deletes the earlier queue entry and the receiving node's pendingReadIndex associates a batch only when the response SystemCtx equals the registered key. The receipts now cover three requesters. In the follower receipt, node 2's admitted context {101,1002} is answered with node 3's later context {202,2003} at log index 4, and node 2's batch stays at index zero after the real ready index 4 is applied; the late confirmation of node 2's own context produces no context-correct reply. The logical-deadline receipt keeps that ordering and shows no completion before the 50-tick deadline, RequestTimeout at tick 51, and removal of the stale batch. The observer-endpoint receipt closes the link that the earlier leader-side observer receipt left open: a real observer peer forwards its own generated context to the real leader, voter 3's later context is confirmed first, the reply addressed to observer 4 carries voter 3's context at log index 4, the observer's real handler emits a ReadyToRead carrying that later context at index 4, and the observer's admitted batch stays at index zero without completing, even after the late own-context confirmation. Both controls complete when the admitted context is confirmed first: the follower control's reply carries its context and its read completes at batch index 4, and the observer control's reply carries the observer's context and its read completes. Because every measured reply carries a later committed index and the ready index equals the applied index, no stale read value or safety violation is established; the established consequence is that an affected client read cannot complete until its deadline even though the leader had a completed confirmation and the node applied a valid ready index. The observer case shows the defect reaches a non-voting client endpoint through the observer's own forwarding and consumer rather than only the leader's outbound message.\",\n \"answers\": {},\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The confirming context returns earlier queued requests while preserving each request's own SystemCtx.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-1\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"Remote replies are tagged with the confirming heartbeat context instead of the queued request's context.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-2\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"A response with a nonmatching SystemCtx leaves the original pending batch at index zero and cannot complete it.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The exercised later-confirmation ordering produced a mismatched reply context and left the earlier read batch unready after the ready index was applied.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"1457862374ac4b5bbba3c0e3588dbb50-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The sequential-confirmation control completed when the admitted context was confirmed first.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"cd8b5340c6da42b49b1358c1b1420aa6-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The logical-deadline case returned RequestTimeout at tick 51 and removed the stale batch.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"68dce962924a4244bd9688bff78649ed-knowledge-1\",\n   \"revision\": 2,\n   \"assertion\": \"Observer-originated ReadIndex requests enter the same leader queue and pending-read response path, and that path is now measured at both the leader-side reply and the observer's own consumer.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The observer leader-side reply carried the later confirming context rather than the observer's admitted context.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"c5d2bc4029e5466da5475db36708ef10-knowledge-1\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The observer's admitted read stayed at index zero and did not complete under the later-first ordering, while the control confirming its own context first completed with batch index 4.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"The source path that constructs the remote reply uses m.Hint and m.HintHigh; no re-tagging occurs between that send and the receiving node's consumer in any measured case.\",\n  \"The main and observer replies carried log index 4 and the ready index was 4, so no execution shows a stale committed index or stale application state.\",\n  \"The late confirmation of the earlier admitted context produced zero context-correct replies and completion remained zero in both the follower and observer cases.\",\n  \"The sequential and observer controls complete with the admitted context, so the failure is not a general inability of the harness, the observer forwarding path, or the pending-read consumer to complete.\",\n  \"The timeout receipt shows a client timeout and cleanup, not a successful stale read; it measures the bounded endpoint without establishing a safety violation.\",\n  \"In the observer-endpoint case the real handler did emit a ReadyToRead at index 4 and that index was applied, so the failure is the missing context association rather than an absent ready signal or an unapplied index.\",\n  \"The observer-endpoint case registers node 4 as an observer through Peer.ApplyConfigChange rather than a proposed membership entry, so it does not establish that a fully replicated observer join changes this path.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"The ILogDB is test-only and in-memory; disk failure, restart, snapshots, and real transport delay were not exercised.\",\n  \"The main test applies the returned ready index synchronously; the companion timeout receipt measures the logical deadline at tick 51, not wall-clock scheduling.\",\n  \"The observer-endpoint receipt exercises a real observer raft peer and the node-level pending-read registry, but not NodeHost request plumbing or the transport, and the observer membership was applied directly to each voter instead of through a committed configuration change.\",\n  \"The controls hold only for their exercised first-context ordering; they do not establish safety or completion for all schedules.\",\n  \"The observed wrong reply context is a correlation defect; it is not by itself evidence that the returned read index is stale or that a wrong data value was read.\",\n  \"The observer-endpoint case measures one observer and one ordering; other membership layouts and concurrent observers were not measured.\"\n ],\n \"joint_history\": \"The follower, sequential-control, and logical-deadline receipts come from the same three-peer in-process harness family; the leader-side observer receipt uses real internal Raft handlers for voters {1,2,3} with observer 4; the observer-endpoint receipt pairs the same three-peer leader with a real observer raft peer plus the node-level pending-read registry. All five experiments sit under the same ReadIndex question and exercise the same leader-side confirmation path. The follower case and both observer cases queue an earlier remote context before a later voter context and confirm the later one first; the two controls confirm the admitted context first; the timeout receipt repeats the later-first ordering with an advanced logical clock. The observer-endpoint receipt supplies the observer local consumer and completion that the leader-side receipt left unmeasured, and it inherits that receipt's ordering while adding the observer peer and the applied observer membership.\",\n \"failure_attribution\": null,\n \"operation_id\": \"c5d2bc4029e5466da5475db36708ef10\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
